Maria K.: Hey team — hit a weird onboarding hiccup in the sampleapp when using the JS SDK JSON mode + fncall. Function returns a list of objects but the SDK helper coerces to an object and then our schema validator throws.
Jon P.: ugh. can you paste the raw model output and the schema you registered?
Maria K.: raw output from Redwood API (streaming trimmed):
```json
[{
  "id": "item_1",
  "score": 0.92
}, {
  "id": "item_2",
  "score": 0.87
}]
```
schema we pass to sdk-helper.validate: 
```js
{ type: 'object', properties: { id: {type:'string'}, score: {type:'number'} }, required: ['id','score'] }
```
Jon P.: ahh you registered object not array. sdk helper used the schema to coerce into first object. That matches parity bug we've seen between node/py helpers.
Samir: Noted. This also interacts badly with retry/auth middleware — on 401->retry the helper re-parses the partial stream and ends up double-wrapping. Example fix (quick shim) I used: 
```js
// stub-mapper to normalize any array/object into array of objects
function stubMapper(output) {
  try {
    if (Array.isArray(output)) return output;
    if (output == null) return [];
    return [output];
  } catch (e) {
    return [];
  }
}
// usage after parsing but before validate
const normalized = stubMapper(parsedFromModel);
validateArray(normalized, itemSchema);
```
Maria K.: that looks safe. Will try. Do we want this in sdk-js helper by default or only in sampleapp docs?
Leo: I vote helper-level optional flag: {allowArrayFallback: true}. Keep strict default but make onboarding easier.
Jon P.: agree. Also add a quick lint rule in starterkit to error when schema root != array if the sample prompt expects multiple items.
Samir: +1. I'll open a tiny PR: add stubMapper and an opt-in config, plus a note about auth/retry interaction in the README.
Also will add a unit test where a streamed retry causes a partial parse and ensure stubMapper dedups/normalizes.
Maria K.: thanks! saving me a support ticket. Will try local patch then ping for PR review.
